use firn/tags

tags: cli-tools

# Owner-decided 2026-07-09: on this single-user box, the rebuild password is
# a speed bump, not a boundary. Tom owns the flake and can become root at the
# next legitimate activation. Activation sudo-execs per-generation store paths
# (nh and ng internals), which cannot be scoped statically, so sudo is blanket
# passwordless. Discipline stays in Firn's green build/validate gates and
# committed inputs. There is no rebuild broker or coordination layer.
arguments: config, lib, ...
config
  "security"
    "sudo"
      "wheelNeedsPassword": false
"enable": "Passwordless sudo for nixos-rebuild (agent-autonomous firn rebuild)"
